    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20848" root="سن" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِنَّةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِنٌّ</span>, in the last quarter of the paragraph, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِكَّةٌ</span>, meaning
<i>A ploughshare;</i> i. e. the <i>iron thing with which
the ground is ploughed up:</i> (AA, IAar, S, L:
[see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُؤَمَةٌ</span>:]) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِنَنٌ</span>. (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [And] <i>A twoheaded</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَأْسٍ</span> [i. e. <i>hoe</i> or <i>adz</i> or <i>axe</i>]: (K:) or
[its pl.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِنَنٌ</span> signifies [simply] <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُؤُوسٌ</span> [pl. of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَأْسٌ</span>]. (L.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَنَّةٌ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُنَّةٌ</span>, last
sentence.

